Each row corresponds to a chemical compound within a compartment and a biological group (the sole group or an analysed prey species). The audit starts from all prepared chemical records, including compounds later excluded from BMF computation. A compound is excluded if it is missing from a biological compartment or, for PCB and PFAS, at least 80 percent of observations in either compartment are censored. HBCDD isomers are an explicit exploratory exception to the 80 percent censoring rule. Gamma parameters are reported only when fitting succeeds; censored values otherwise receive the predefined LOQ/2 fallback. The count and percentage variables are based on analytical records, not independent fish.
